<article class="env-corollary" id="06MH">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06MH">Corollary <span data-tag="06MH">7.4.1.19</span>.</a> Let $U: \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be a left fibration of $\infty $-categories which admits a covariant transport representation $\operatorname{Tr}_{\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}/\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{S}}$ and let $F: K^{\triangleleft } \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be a limit diagram. The following conditions are equivalent: </p>
<p><dl>
<dt>$(1)$</dt>
<dd><p>
The composition $\operatorname{Tr}_{\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}/\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}} \circ F$ is a limit diagram in the $\infty $-category of spaces $\operatorname{\mathcal{S}}$. 
</p>
</dd>
<dt>$(2)$</dt>
<dd><p>
Every lifting problem 
</p>
<div class="equation" id="06MJ">
<span class="equation-label"><a data-tag="06MJ" href="/tag/06MJ">7.57</a></span>
<div>\begin{equation}  \begin{gathered}\label{equation:improvement-scheme4} \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ K \ar [r]^-{ \widetilde{F}_0} \ar [d] &amp;  \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}\ar [d]^{U} \\ K^{\triangleleft } \ar [r]^-{F} \ar@ {--&gt;}[ur]^{ \widetilde{F} } &amp;  \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}} \end{gathered} \end{equation}</div>
</div>
<p>
 admits a solution, where $\widetilde{F}$ is a limit diagram in the $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}$. 
</p>
</dd>
</dl></p>
<p> Moreover, if this condition is satisfied, then every diagram $\widetilde{F}: K^{\triangleleft } \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}$ satisfying $U \circ \widetilde{F} = F$ is a limit diagram in $\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      Combine Corollaries <a data-tag="06MF" href="/tag/06MF">7.4.1.18</a> and <a data-tag="02KR" href="/tag/02KR">7.1.6.12</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
</article>
